elf.propagation_log.append({\n            \"parent_request_id\": parent_context.get(\"request_id\"),\n            \"parent_correlation_id\": parent_context.get(\"correlation_id\"),\n            \"child_keys\": list(child.keys()),\n        })\n        return child\n```\n\nNow I need to escape this properly for JSON. The key challenge is handling the quotes and newlines in the docstring and code. I need to complete the JSON string by escaping all the special characters properly. The docstring contains multiple lines and quotes that need careful handling - each `\"` becomes `\\\"`, newlines become `\\n`, and any backslashes become `\\\\`. \n\nLooking at the structure, I'm building a JSON object with a \"code\" key containing the full method as an escaped string, plus a \"comments\" key. The method definition spans from the function signature through the return statement, with the docstring explaining the context propagation logic and noting the bug where `correlation_id` gets dropped. The fix involves ensuring both `request_id` and `correlation_id` are included in the child context dictionary that gets returned, and logging both parent identifiers along with the child keys for traceability.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4442,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4442},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0aab4cc-6bdd-4a19-a494-3c93ac46cf72","uuid":"351e75d9-f9d1-4c85-b0a7-8ca38583f6f5"}
